    "The complete RAG pipeline combines dense retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, and transformer-based zero-shot classification. For each question, the top-k documents are first retrieved from the knowledge base using FAISS. These documents are then reranked using a Cross-Encoder, and the highest-ranked document is appended as additional context before performing zero-shot classification. This enables the model to answer questions using both retrieved knowledge and its internal reasoning capabilities."
